<div class="w-50" style="text-align: center; padding-left: 50px; padding-right: 50px;">
<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #ffffff;" href="https://cdnsm5-ss20.sharpschool.com/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/Community/Referendum/ReferendumFAQ261023.pdf" title="Link to the Frequently Asked Questions: PCPS Ballot Referendum">
<div style="text-decoration: none; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: rgb(0, 40, 85); width: 100%; max-width: 600px; text-align: center; border-radius: 25px; margin-top: 50px;">
<p style="text-decoration: none; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); padding: 10px; font-size: 20px;"><strong>Frequently Asked Questions: School Ballot Initiative</strong></p>
</div>
</a>
<div style="padding: 10px 0 10px -50px;"><a style="text-decoration: none; color: #ffffff;" href="https://cdnsm5-ss20.sharpschool.com/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/Community/Referendum/2026SchoolBallotInitiativePresentation260821.pdf" title="Link to the Tax Referendum Presentation">
<div style="background-color: #002855; color: #ffffff; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; text-align: center; border-radius: 25px;">
<p style="text-decoration: none; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); padding: 10px; font-size: 20px;"><strong>School Ballot Initiative Presentation</strong></p>
</div>
</a>
</div>
</div>
</div></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl11_divContent"><div style="margin-top: 50px;">
<a href="/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/About%20PCPS/About%20the%20District/PCPSBudgetGuide2627.pdf"><img src="https://cdnsm5-ss20.sharpschool.com/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/About%20PCPS/About%20the%20District/BudgetGuide26-27.jpg" alt="2026-227 PCPS Budget Guide" title="2026-227 PCPS Budget Guide" style="float: left; margin: 20px 40px 40px 40px; border: 1px solid #000; width: 180px;"></a>
<div id="stateofthedistrict" style="background-color: #e1f2fe; padding: 40px 40px 0 40px;">
<h2>PCPS Budget Guide Now Available!</h2>
<p>Ever wonder what it takes to efficiently manage our school district’s budget?</p>
<p>The PCPS Budget Guide provides a brief overview of our local school system’s financial priorities and challenges.</p>
<p>Our school district is one of the lowest funded districts in the state, but PCPS continues to operate fiscally responsible and maintain a focus on instructional services and operational efficiency.<span style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<div style="overflow-x:auto;">
<div class="w-100 w-row" style="text-align: center; margin: auto;">
<div class="w-50" style="text-align: center;">
<div style="background-color: #002855; color: #ffffff; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; text-align: center; border-radius: 25px;">
<p style="text-decoration: none; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); padding: 10px; font-size: 20px;"><strong><a style="text-decoration: none; color: #ffffff;" href="/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/About%20PCPS/About%20the%20District/PCPSBudgetGuide2627.pdf">2026-27&nbsp;PCPS Budget Guide </a></strong></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl14_divContent"><div style="margin-top: 50px;"></div>
<a href="https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/community/taxreferendum#stateofthedistrict"><img src="https://cdnsm5-ss20.sharpschool.com/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/Community/Newsletter/2026/January/StateOfTheDistrictIcon.jpg" alt="State of the District Preview Image" title="State of the District Preview Image" style="float: right; margin: 20px; border: 1px solid #000; width: 200px;"></a>
<div id="stateofthedistrict" style="background-color: #e1f2fe; padding: 40px 40px 0 40px;">
<h2>State of the District Annual Report </h2>
<p>Do you want to learn more about how the hard work and dedication of PCPS students and staff is leading to success?<span style="font-family: arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p>The State of the District Report provides an in-depth look into the complexities of PCPS, the second largest employer in Polk County and one of the largest school districts in the nation.</p>
<div style="overflow-x:auto;">
<div class="w-100 w-row" style="text-align: center; margin: auto;">
<div class="w-50" style="text-align: center;">
<div style="background-color: #002855; color: #ffffff; width: 100%; max-width: 600px; text-align: center; border-radius: 25px;">
<p style="text-decoration: none; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); padding: 10px; font-size: 20px;"><strong>"<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #ffffff;" href="https://cdnsm5-ss20.sharpschool.com/UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/About PCPS/StateOfTheDistrict/StateOfTheDistrict260205.pdf">State of the District” annual report for 2024-2025</a></strong></p>
<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #ffffff;" href="UserFiles/Servers/Server_3007318/Image/Community/Referendum/ReferendumFAQ251201.pdf">
</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl17_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">What is the school district proposing?</h2>
<p>Polk County Public Schools is asking voters to consider approving a 1.0 ad valorem millage rate increase on the upcoming ballot. This funding would support the recruitment and retention of school-based employees and protect critical student programs (fine arts, school safety, workforce development and early childhood education).</p>
<p>In short, this referendum is about people, students, and the future of Polk County’s workforce and communities.</p>
<p>It ensures safe schools, competitive staffing and well-rounded educational opportunities.</p></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl20_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">Ballot Language Approved by The Polk County School Board</h2></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl23_divContent"><p>Ballot Language. The School Board adopts the following ballot title and summary for placement on the November 3, 2026, general election ballot:</p>
<p>Title: Millage for School Safety, Teachers, and Career Education<br>
Ballot Summary: Shall the Polk County School District levy an additional 1.0 mill in ad valorem taxes annually to fund school operations for teacher recruitment and retention and education support staff, for career and technical education, school safety, arts, and early learning—with proceeds shared with charter schools as required by law and monitored by an independent citizens' oversight committee?</p></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl26_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">Why now?</h2>
<p>Polk County’s population growth, staffing shortages, rising costs and competition from other counties make this a critical moment. Without action, the quality of educational services and staffing stability will continue to decline.</p></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl29_divContent"><h2 style="margin-top: 50px;">Revenue Summary</h2></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl32_divContent"><p><strong>If approved, how much money will this generate for the school district?</strong></p>
<p>If approved, PCPS is projected to receive approximately $65.6 million. The funding would be spent as follows:</p>
<ul>
    <li>80% used to fund additional compensation for all employees ($52.5M)</li>
    <li>20% used to provide funding to support ($13.1M)
    <ul>
        <li>School Safety and Security</li>
        <li>Fine/Performing Arts</li>
        <li>Workforce Development/Career Tech Education</li>
        <li>Early Childhood Education</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
</ul></div>
</div><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div>
<style type="text/css">
    .disabledIco {
        color: lightgrey;
    }
</style>
<div id="tabPortlet_212590" data-clientId="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35" class="PO-wrapper PO-tabAccordion">
    
    
    <div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_upPanel">
	
            <div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabs" role="region" style="width:100%;" class="TA-accordionMode" portlet="accordion" aria-label="Accordion Portlet">
                
            </div>
        
</div>
    
    <label for="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabEdit" aria-hidden="true"  Style="display: none">tab visible</label>
    <input name="ctl00$ContentPlaceHolder1$ctl35$divTabEdit" type="text" value="True" id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabEdit" class="divTabEdit" style="display: none" />
    
</div>

<script type="text/javascript">
    
	$(document).ready(function () {
		var logConsole = function (str) {
			console.log(str);
		};
		if ($('#tabPortlet_212590 .divTabEdit').val() == "True") {
			var isModern = ('True');
			if (isModern.toLowerCase() == "true") {
				var tabObj = $('#tabPortlet_212590 ');
				var tabM = $('#ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabs').attr('portlet') == 'tab';

				function activate() {
					$(tabObj).scrollingTabs({
						tabs: [{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabs_0","title":"Will Charter Schools Receive Funding?","content":"<style>\n    table {\n    font-family: arial, sans-serif;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n    }\n    td, th {\n    border: 1px solid #dddddd;\n    text-align: left;\n    padding: 8px;\n    }\n    tr:nth-child(even) {\n    background-color: #dddddd;\n    }\n</style>\n<p>Yes, charter schools will receive funding as required by law.</p>\n<p>If approved, charter schools would receive approximately $13.6 million based on enrollment.</p>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabs_1","title":"Polk County Public Schools Portion","content":"<style>\n    table {\n    font-family: arial, sans-serif;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n    }\n    td, th {\n    border: 1px solid #dddddd;\n    text-align: left;\n    padding: 8px;\n    }\n    tr:nth-child(even) {\n    background-color: #dddddd;\n    }\n</style>\n<p>If approved, PCPS is projected to receive approximately $65.6 million. The funding would be spent as follows:<br>\n<br>\n80% used to fund additional compensation for all employees ($52.5M)<br>\n20% used to provide funding to support ($13.1M)<br>\nSchool Safety and Security<br>\nFine/Performing Arts<br>\nWorkforce Development/Career Tech Education<br>\nEarly Childhood Education</p>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl35_divTabs_2","title":"Examples of Other District Allocations","content":"<style>\n    table {\n    font-family: arial, sans-serif;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n    }\n    td, th {\n    border: 1px solid #dddddd;\n    text-align: left;\n    padding: 8px;\n    }\n    tr:nth-child(even) {\n    background-color: #dddddd;\n    }\n</style>\n<p><strong>What can employees expect if the taxpayers approve this referendum? How much additional money might they get?</strong></p>\n<p>The final amount that each employee can expect must be bargained. However, here are some comparisons that show how other districts have allocated funds from their referendums.</p>\n<div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\n<table>\n    <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th>District</th>\n            <th>Teachers (annual)</th>\n            <th>Support/ESP (annual unless noted)</th>\n            <th>Bus and Transportation</th>\n            <th>Administrators</th>\n            <th>Notes&nbsp;</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td><strong>Hillsborough</strong></td>\n            <td>$6,000 supplement</td>\n            <td>$3,000 supplement</td>\n            <td>Included in support</td>\n            <td>$6,000 supplement</td>\n            <td>&nbsp;</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><strong>Pinellas</strong></td>\n            <td>$6,967 supplement (2024-25)</td>\n            <td>Supplement added starting 2024-25 (amount varies by role; district materials don’t show a single flat figure)</td>\n            <td>Included in support</td>\n            <td>Not included (referendum focuses on teachers + support)</td>\n            <td><a href=\"https://www.pcsb.org/page/11278\" title=\"Link to Pinellas County Schools Website\">Voters renewed and expanded the mill to 1.0; teachers’ exact supplement published, support supplement authorized but published amounts vary by job.&nbsp;</a></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><strong>Pasco</strong></td>\n            <td>$2,000–$7,245 (tiered by years of service)</td>\n            <td>$0.80–$3.50 per hour (tiered by district service years)</td>\n            <td>Presumed 8 hours/day for annual calc (district rule)</td>\n            <td>Not eligible (millage excludes admin)</td>\n            <td><a href=\"https://www.pasco.k12.fl.us/library/er/MOU-Instructional_Referendum_Implementation.pdf\" title=\"Link to Pasco Schools Website\">All paid as non-recurring “referendum salary supplements,” bargained annually.</a></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><strong>Brevard</strong></td>\n            <td>Example shown publicly: ~$7,849 millage add-on for a ~20-year teacher (amounts vary by table/experience)</td>\n            <td>Yes — millage supplements paid to “all eligible employee groups” (amounts vary by bargaining unit) </td>\n            <td>Included as eligible groups</td>\n            <td>Non-bargaining also receive millage supplements (varies)</td>\n            <td><a href=\"https://www.floridatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/11/08/brevard-voters-signal-support-increasing-school-tax-rate-teacher-raises-millage/10604985002/\" title=\"Link to Florida Today Website\">Voters approved 1 mill in 2022; district pays millage supplements over 20 pay periods.</a></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><strong>Orange</strong></td>\n            <td>No fixed per-employee supplement publicly posted from millage</td>\n            <td>No fixed per-employee supplement</td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center;);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center;);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td><a href=\"https://mynews13.com/fl/orlando/news/2022/08/22/orange-county-voters-to-decide-whether-to-renew-one-mill-property-tax\" title=\"Link to Spectrum News 13 Website\">OCPS’ long-standing 1-mill funds program staffing (arts/athletics, retention supports, counselors, etc.); not published as flat individual supplements.</a></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>Osceola</td>\n            <td>&nbsp;No current 1-mill operating referendum → no millage supplements</td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;—</td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center; background-color: rgb(221, 221, 221);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center; background-color: rgb(221, 221, 221);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td><a href=\"https://www.positivelyosceola.com/osceola-school-board-approves-tentative-budget-recognizes-heritage-civil-rights-civic-education-and-ese-changes/\" title=\"Link to Positively Osceola Website\">Compensation handled via regular bargaining; board discussions reference potential future millage but none in force now.</a></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>Lee</td>\n            <td>&nbsp;No operating millage for pay (separate district incentives exist)<br>\n            </td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center;);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center;);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: arial, sans-serif; text-align: center;);\">&nbsp;—</span></td>\n            <td>&nbsp;</td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>","active":false,"disabled":false}],// required,
						propPaneId: 'paneId', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propTitle: 'title', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propActive: 'active', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propDisabled: 'disabled', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propContent: 'content', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						tabMode: tabM,
						scrollToTabEdge: false, // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						disableScrollArrowsOnFullyScrolled: false // optional- pass in default value for demo purposes
					}).on('ready.scrtabs', function () {
						$('#' + this.id + ' .tab-pane').attr('tabindex', 0);
					});
				};

				activate();

            }
        }
	});

